  message: "DONE in PR #1873 (merged, dev 4f8898915e). Prose only, no behaviour change; every corrected sentence was checked against the code it describes. Fixed: ddg_mixed = covered but not confirmed (not_attempted or escaped; refuted flows are removed) in TaintFlowFinding.analysis_method, UNADJUDICATED_METHODS, ClaimVerdict.analysis_methods, the evidence-row comment and spec §15 (per method_for_walk_verdict); unavailable = the walk did NOT run (dataflow_scope); precise = walk confirmed only (propagate docstring); envelope 2.3 comment (walk_verdicts.unconfirmed always 0 over findings); ClaimVerdict.evidence / evidence_count for the sink_before_source-only confirmed_with_caveats (deferred flows, >= 1); CONFIRMING_VERDICTS (the CLI compares literals); exit-3 and '!' rationale (16 caveat kinds, most analysis limits); cmd_verify_claims zone list and TaintSink.zone examples; 'every built-in sink comes from io_primitives' in cli/taint/verify_claims (false since ADR-0060); 'no bash catalogue' in io_boundary_types/verify_claims (bash.yaml covers the shell's own redirections). docs/concept-axes.md regenerated (the command_launch description is registry-sourced); docs/schema.json regenerated byte-identical.\n\nCHECK ON MERGED DEV: grep of packages/hypergumbo-core/src + spec + concept-axes for 'the walk ran and did not confirm', 'the walk ran but the DDG held no', 'no bash catalogue', 'Trust zones checked:', '0 if confirmed', \"the CLI's exit code and the CLI's\", 'walk ran without confirming' -> no hits.\n\nRESIDUAL (not in the filed list; one word): load_full_taint_catalog's docstring (taint.py ~2600) says 'Built-in sinks come entirely from layer 2' and then, in the same sentence, that ADR-0060 restores taint_sinks/ for non-boundary sinks -- 'entirely' is wrong. Fix in the next PR that touches taint.py. Split out earlier: bakeoff-deep's == 'confirmed' count -> WI-fomif. WI-bujum's rename will rewrite several of these sentences; they are correct for today's names."  # dc3f
